{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116915","id":3340105341,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7HFfZ9","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116915","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116915.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116915.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116915","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116915/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116915/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116915/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/4df16a44fbe34c6e9c3322bc7d28ab92dc28a3ef","number":116915,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add 'layer_mask' property to 'Material'","user":{"login":"ramblingstranger","id":114190975,"node_id":"U_kgDOBs5qfw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114190975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger","html_url":"https://github.com/ramblingstranger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramblingstranger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR adds a `layer_mask` property to `Material`, which can be used to select which visual layers an individual material will render on. Like with `render_priority`, this property is only available for subclasses of `BaseMaterial3D` and for `ShaderMaterial` with a spatial shader.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"430\" height=\"601\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6f209dc-d66a-475b-b636-3df53b812ba5\" />\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\n*Implements and closes <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11210>.*\r\n\r\nSomething similar to this could already be accomplished in Godot shaders through use of `CAMERA_VISIBLE_LAYERS`. However, this PR enables this functionality in `StandardMaterial3D` and `ORMMaterial3D`. Also, even for shader materials, it should provide faster layer-based culling than could be accomplished with `CAMERA_VISIBLE_LAYERS` since the material is culled before the draw call. Combined with the ability to add more materials via `next_pass`, this gives users a greater level of control over how their objects render on different layers.\r\n\r\n## Related Work\r\n\r\n*Supersedes <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99565>.*\r\n\r\nI originally implemented this same feature by modifying the generated shader code for `BaseMaterial3D` to cull based on `CAMERA_VISIBLE_LAYERS`. However, in that PR, it was suggested that I look into doing this before the draw call by passing the layer mask to the rendering server.\r\n\r\n## Technical Overview\r\n\r\nThe culling currently happens in the `_fill_render_list()` method for each renderer. As far as I could tell, this is the first place where there is a list with elements that correspond to individual materials. Prior to that, such as in `RenderSceneCull`, all lists contain complete geometry instances, and so it is not possible to cull individual materials.\r\n\r\nBefore culling, the code checks to make sure that it is in the color pass. Without this check, I noticed that shadows were broken on Forward+ and Mobile. I could use some feedback about this part since I don't know what should be expected for each type of pass, whether the material should be culled or not. (Note: Even without this check, shadows were not broken on Compatibility. The distinction seems to be that Compatibility defaults `RenderDataGLES3::camera_visible_layers` to 0xFFFFFFFF, while Forward+ and Mobile do not provide a default value for `RenderSceneDataRD::camera_visible_layers`.)","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizat